    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The only test class is `AcceptanceTest` (the other two files are helpers), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-duplicate detection for owner creation, per the spec: a new owner that isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` + `postcode` with a *different* telephone is still created, and returns `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges, each kept in the layer where it belongs:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added two persistent fields `possibleDuplicate` (`Boolean`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (`Integer`) with columns `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of`, plus getters/setters. These must persist because the test reads them back via a later `GET`.\n\n2. **`ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 stamped the flags at creation time inside the existing `saveOwner(...)` `owner.isNew()` block, right alongside the other creation-time derivations (namesake count, bulk-signup warning, household size), so all creation-stamping stays in one place. Added a small private helper `findPossibleDuplicate(Owner)` that reuses the existing `findByLastNameIgnoreCase` finder, filters by equal postcode and different telephone, and picks the earliest matching owner. No public API/interface change was needed, and no new repository method (reused an existing one).\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` response schema; MapStruct maps them automatically by name.\n\n4. **Schema files** \u2014 added the two columns to the `owners` table in all four DB schemas (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus `h2`, `postgres`, `mysql` for consistency).\n\nThe soft check runs after the existing hard-duplicate (identity-key) check, so hard duplicates still get a 409 and only non-duplicate creates reach the soft-flagging path.",
